 Backend secrets — copy to .env and fill in. Everything is OPTIONAL for local dev;
 the app boots with safe defaults (SQLite, no Firebase, no email).
 The .env file lives at the repo root and is loaded by pydantic-settings.

 --- Database ---
Default already points at ./interviai.db (SQLite). Override for Postgres:
 DATABASE_URL=postgresql+asyncpg://user:pass@localhost:5432/interviai

 --- Firebase Auth (optional in dev; auth endpoints will reject if missing) ---
 FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON='{"type":"service_account",...}'
 GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS_PATH=C:\path\to\serviceAccount.json
FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=interv-ai-880ac
 --- Firebase Storage (optional) ---
 FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=interv-ai-880ac.appspot.com

 --- Gemini AI (optional — used by /api/ai/* endpoints) ---
 GEMINI_API_KEY=your-key-here
 GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.1-pro-preview

 --- Outbound email (optional — welcome message after onboarding) ---
 SMTP_USER=you@gmail.com
 SMTP_PASSWORD=your-app-password
 ADMIN_EMAIL=you@gmail.com

 --- Frontend origin (CORS). Default is fine for local dev. ---
 FRONTEND_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3000
 APP_URL=http://localhost:3000
/